Day 7 — Dictionaries Deep Dive

Easy:
Count frequency of each word in a sentence using a dictionary; 
Create a dictionary from two lists (keys, values) using zip();
Find the key with the maximum value in a dictionary; 
Check if a key exists in a dictionary;
Merge two dictionaries into one
Medium:
Invert a dictionary (swap keys and values);
Sort a dictionary by keys alphabetically;
Find all keys that have a specific value;
Count character frequency in a string using a dictionary;
Create a dictionary of squares for numbers 1-10 using comprehension
Tough:
Group a list of words by their first letter into a dictionary of lists;
Find the most common word in a paragraph without using Counter;
Build a nested dictionary representing a simple student database (name → {marks, age}); 
Merge two dictionaries, summing values for common keys;
Implement a simple word-frequency counter that ignores punctuation and case
